WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.161
The fix is one line.

00:00:02.161 --> 00:00:06.324
Codex changes the allowed metrics port from
9091 to 9090,

00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:08.405
where the service actually listens.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.445
GitLab built, scanned, and published the
service image.

00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:15.137
Argo CD synced the deployment in Azure.

00:00:15.137 --> 00:00:19.234
We replay the policy change on local
Kubernetes to test the repair.

00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:22.649
With the wrong port, Prometheus marks the
target down.

00:00:22.649 --> 00:00:25.437
The same pod still answers its health check.

00:00:25.713 --> 00:00:29.370
The plugin renders the chart before and after
the edit.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.563
All six resources pass schema validation.

00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:33.213
Compare the policies.

00:00:33.213 --> 00:00:35.491
Only the ingress port changed.

00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:39.543
The namespace and pod selectors still restrict
access to Prometheus.

00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:42.772
The deployment branch now points to the
corrected policy.

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:46.851
Argo CD syncs that commit and applies the new
port in Kubernetes.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.596
The scrape is back.

00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:50.769
Prometheus goes from 0 to 1,

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:53.667
and fresh samples show the event counter
increasing.

00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:55.500
The pod kept serving.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.830
The unauthorized probe is still blocked.
